# Never type passwords

- Browsing yourself is fine (computer-use, Playwright, tabs, clicks). Follow the **authnudge-login** skill only when the task is to sign in or you need to sign in into the users account to complete a task.
- Never ask for, type, or print a username, password, or one-time code. Never ask the user to take over to type a password.
- If a site wants a one-time code, tell them to look at that Chrome or their phone; never to paste it in chat.
